      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Comorbidity between headache and other disorders such as psychological or memory problems is a topic of increasing scientific interest both for us diagnostic and therapeutic implications but also for pathogenetic advances. A central neurogenic mechanism such as a dysregulation of some neurotransmitter system might underlie not only headache but also other coexistent disorders; findings highlight the role of serotonin pathways."},
